{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1935"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge art/painting","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/art__painting.g1.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",251],["+"," Friedrich died in Dresden in 1840 and lies buried in the city's Trinitatisfriedhof."],["=",149],["+","The movement's ties to literature ran deep. Ludwig Emil Grimm (1790–1863), the younger brother of the fairy-tale collectors Jacob and Wilhelm Grimm, was no philologist but a painter and etcher: he taught at the Kassel academy, drew the portraits of his brothers that everyone knows, and illustrated editions of their Children's and Household Tales.\n\n"],["=",482],["-","five"],["+","of"],["=",1],["+","them "],["=",45]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",235],["+"," Friedrich starb 1840 in Dresden und ist auf dem dortigen Trinitatisfriedhof begraben."],["=",137],["+","Die Verbindungen der Bewegung zur Literatur waren eng. Ludwig Emil Grimm (1790–1863), der jüngere Bruder der Märchensammler Jacob und Wilhelm Grimm, war kein Philologe, sondern Maler und Radierer: Er lehrte an der Kasseler Akademie, zeichnete die bekannten Porträts seiner Brüder und illustrierte Ausgaben ihrer Kinder- und Hausmärchen.\n\n"],["=",454],["-","fünf "],["=",45]]}]},
